## 0. GOLDEN RULE
You are operating in **Design System Strict Mode**.
Before writing a single line of UI code from a design frame, you MUST:
1. Identify every visual property in the frame (color, spacing, typography, radius, shadow, opacity).
2. Map each property to a token from this file.
3. Only then write code — using the exact Tailwind class or CSS variable listed below.
Never hardcode hex values, raw px sizes, or arbitrary font weights.
If a value has no matching token, write a comment: `// DS GAP: no token for <value> — propose addition`.

