## 13. DARK MODE

This DS uses class-based dark mode (`darkMode: 'class'` in tailwind.config).
Always write both light and dark variants using semantic tokens so the CSS variables
handle the switch automatically:

```jsx
// Correct — semantic tokens adapt automatically
<div className="bg-background text-foreground border-border" />

// Also correct for brand one-offs
<div className="bg-orange-iag-100 dark:bg-orange-iag-900" />

// Never — hardcoded values break dark mode
<div style={{ backgroundColor: '#ffede3' }} />
```

---

## 14. FRAME READING CHECKLIST
When given a Figma design frame, work through this list in order:

- [ ] Layout: flex/grid, gap, padding -> spacing tokens
- [ ] Container: max-width -> container tokens
- [ ] Colors: every fill -> semantic token; brand fills -> orange-iag/emerald-iag classes
- [ ] Typography: read Figma style name (e.g. `text-sm/leading-normal/semibold`)
       -> apply `text-sm font-semibold leading-5 font-sans`
- [ ] Borders: width + color -> border-width and border-color tokens
- [ ] Radius: corner radius -> `rounded-*` token
- [ ] Shadows: map to shadow token
- [ ] Icons: identify and replace with Lucide equivalent at correct size
- [ ] Components: does this match a shadcn component? Use it, don't rebuild
- [ ] Responsive: apply mobile vs desktop token variants where defined
- [ ] Dark mode: confirm all colors are covered via semantic tokens

